      "content": "You must conduct a comprehensive audit across all data storage environments, including legacy systems, archive logs, and shadow databases, to verify no residual data remains. Legal liability extends to all places the controller (you) is reasonably expected to store the data, meaning you are responsible for ensuring deletion even in technically difficult or hidden locations. If you discover such data but cannot delete it, you must carefully document your efforts to eradicate it and assess the proportionality of the remaining risk before formally informing the data subject.\n\nRemember that records of processing activities should map these \"deep dive\" checks to your data inventory to prove compliance during audits. Failing to eliminate data from these hidden repositories can still constitute a violation, even if the original deletion from the primary system was successful.",
